{"source": "designer", "id": 65, "type": "plan", "message": "Wrote designs/wall_bracket.py: an L-shaped shelf bracket modelled shelf-face-down (z=0 shelf face, x=0 wall face, centred on Y). The L is one XZ profile with the inner and outer corner fillets applied to the sketch before extrusion; the four free plate corners get the plan corner radius. A centreline triangular gusset (reach as a share of each free leg, ramp edges filleted before the union, overlapping into the legs' mid-planes) carries the load and leaves both screw pairs clear. Shelf screws are M4 counterbores from z=thickness via counterbored_hole(); wall screws are horizontal M4 teardrop counterbores from the room face via counterbored_hole(teardrop=True), peak print-up, so nothing needs support. All hardware sizes come from standard_parts(); every cutter and the gusset is wrapped in feature(). Harness check: gates 1-4 PASS (7/7 hard dims within \u00b10.1, watertight, support risk 0.9 %), sweep 31/31 PASS with no dead params."}
